closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":9,"created_at":"2026-04-24T15:06:54Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T21:25:45Z","closed_at":"2026-05-07T21:25:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.7 double precision, custom fork: 292b5db1f\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev.mono.double (292b5db1f) - Pop!_OS 22.04 LTS on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 580.126.18) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.26 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using this custom wandering grass shader in Godot 4.7 with double supper, certain viewing angles causes the particles to shift / disappear.  At first I thought it was a culling issue, but further testing seems to indicate the shift can be a large shift offscreen compared to a small shift as seen in the following videos.  Below are some comparisons with single precision which works perfectly compared to double precision which is when the issues arise.\n\n### Single Precision Editor View ✅\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e09e2f1-b32e-42c8-bdc6-3e3ec1b72485\n\n### Double Precision Editor View ❌\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/10d60db8-73ef-4384-9214-52197bce14bf\n\n### Single Precision In Game ✅\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/313d17a2-3c14-4279-9d92-585e0e99694c\n\n### Double Precision In Game ❌\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d62c94df-b7dd-4bf3-ba0a-632ea7719ebd\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Build godot with double precision \n1. Open the MRP\n1. Open the wandering_grass.tscn\n1. Move the editor camera up to the edge of the z or x axis\n1. Look left and right and see that the grass shifts / disappears\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27057060/mrp.zip)\n\nEdit:\n\nChanged h265 videos to h264.  Quality is degraded, but it should play on everyone's devices now.  I thought GitHub would stream regardless of encoding.  Didn't realize that wasn't the case.  Thank you for pointing that out @matheusmdx ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118918/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118918/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}